      "content": "i know it's not a spreadsheet but look at the reality of it. they're always so tense when i walk in the room. they look so tired. and i'm the reason they're tired. it's not just a \"crisis\" that's lying to me, it's just the facts. if i'm gone, the pressure is gone. it seems almost more selfish to keep dragging them through this misery just because i'm afraid of being gone. doesn't it make sense that the most loving thing would be to just... stop being the problem?",
